Building a .NET 8 Application in Harness CI on OpenShift
  
Objective:
The objective of this POC is to validate the ability to build a .NET 8 application using Harness CI with OpenShift Container Platform (OCP) as the build infrastructure.

The setup uses:
OpenShift Sandbox Cluster
Namespace: paisandy-dev
Harness Delegate deployed inside OpenShift
Kubernetes Direct Build Infrastructure
Docker Hub / Microsoft Container Registry public image (mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0)
OpenShift RBAC for CI build pod creation

Architecture Overview:
Harness CI
    |
    |
Harness Delegate
(OpenShift Namespace: paisandy-dev)
    |
    |
Creates Build Pods
    |
    |
.NET SDK Container
(mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0)
    |
    |
Build / Restore / Test / Publish

Prerequisites:
Before starting the POC, the following prerequisites were available:
OpenShift Sandbox Cluster access
Project/Namespace: paisandy-dev
Harness account
Delegate Token generated from Harness
Access to Docker Hub/Microsoft Container Registry
OpenShift CLI (oc) access

Step 1: Deploy Harness Delegate
A Kubernetes Delegate was deployed in the paisandy-dev namespace.

Delegate Deployment yaml as below:
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  labels:
    harness.io/name: kubernetes-delegate
  name: kubernetes-delegate
  namespace: paisandy-dev
spec:
  replicas: 1
  minReadySeconds: 120
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      harness.io/name: kubernetes-delegate
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        harness.io/name: kubernetes-delegate
      annotations:
        prometheus.io/scrape: "true"
        prometheus.io/port: "3460"
        prometheus.io/path: "/api/metrics"
    spec:
      terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 3600
      restartPolicy: Always
      containers:
      - image: us-docker.pkg.dev/gar-prod-setup/harness-public/harness/delegate:26.05.89101
        imagePullPolicy: Always
        name: delegate
        ports:
          - containerPort: 8080
        envFrom:
        - secretRef:
            name: kubernetes-delegate-account-token
        env:
        - name: JAVA_OPTS
          value: "-Xms64M"
        - name: ACCOUNT_ID
          value: 6G-OAYZ5RLO1HiCYOun12w
        - name: MANAGER_HOST_AND_PORT
          value: https://app.harness.io
        - name: DEPLOY_MODE
          value: KUBERNETES
        - name: DELEGATE_NAME
          value: kubernetes-delegate
        - name: DELEGATE_TYPE
          value: "KUBERNETES"
        - name: DELEGATE_NAMESPACE
          valueFrom:
            fieldRef:
              fieldPath: metadata.namespace
        - name: INIT_SCRIPT
          value: ""
        - name: DELEGATE_DESCRIPTION
          value: ""
        - name: DELEGATE_TAGS
          value: ""
        - name: NEXT_GEN
          value: "true"
        - name: CLIENT_TOOLS_DOWNLOAD_DISABLED
          value: "true"
        - name: DELEGATE_RESOURCE_THRESHOLD
          value: ""
        - name: DYNAMIC_REQUEST_HANDLING
          value: "false"

Step 2: Configure OpenShift RBAC

Harness CI requires permissions to create and manage build pods inside the namespace.

Create Role:
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: harness-ci-builder
  namespace: paisandy-dev
rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods", "secrets", "configmaps", "services", "events"]
    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch", "create", "update", "patch", "delete"]
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods/log"]
    verbs: ["get", "list"]

Create Role Binding:
The role was mapped to the default service account.
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: harness-ci-builder
  namespace: paisandy-dev
subjects:
  - kind: ServiceAccount
    name: default
    namespace: paisandy-dev
roleRef:
  kind: Role
  name: harness-ci-builder
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io

